  "summary": "Toledo City Council introduced legislation for an independent audit of the city's Flock Safety ALPR cameras, to be conducted by the city auditor and potentially voted on Sept. 22. The audit would review searches, sharing arrangements, retention, and misuse controls but would not pause the cameras during the review, despite some council members' requests.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Residents have expressed concerns regarding the use, access, and sharing of information through the Flock system under the control or supervision of the city of Toledo",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "I think it is imperative, at this point, that the administration pause the use of this technology until we find out how to better protect our residents",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    },
    {
      "quote": "from June 20 to July 20, more than 904,000 searches were conducted by more than 3,200 agencies",
      "paragraph_idx": 19
    }
  ],
